<section class="block-section story">
  <span class="section-tag">Story</span>
  <h2>What this page is about</h2>
  <p class="sub">Take-home 2, part 2. The other major hazard family.</p>
  <figure class="content-figure">
    <img src="/assets/img/u3/u3-t2-cover.jpg" alt="">
    <figcaption>Image generated with Gemini, AISC. Decorative, not a diagram.</figcaption>
  </figure>
  <p>So far we've talked about earthquakes and tsunamis. This page adds volcanism: why volcanoes line up above a subduction zone, and why those volcanoes tend to explode. And here is the hard part: <strong>some hazards have no engineering defense.</strong> You can't build a wall against a pyroclastic flow. Only distance and early warning save lives.</p>
</section>

